# Fuzzing (contracts/fuzz)
#
# Two things here are deliberately NOT ignored, and it is worth stating why:
#
#   contracts/fuzz/fuzz_targets/*.rs   the targets themselves - these are the
#                                      deliverable and must be committed.
#   contracts/fuzz/Cargo.toml          the target declarations - likewise.
#
# What is ignored is generated state. `corpus/` is libFuzzer's accumulated
# coverage: it is large, it is per-machine noise, and the CI workflow caches and
# restores it explicitly rather than storing it in git. `artifacts/` holds crash
# reproducers, which are useful when they are attached to an issue or uploaded
# as a CI artifact and actively harmful in the repository, since a stale crash
# input sitting in-tree looks like a current failure.
contracts/fuzz/target/
contracts/fuzz/corpus/
contracts/fuzz/artifacts/
contracts/fuzz/coverage/
contracts/fuzz/proptests/target/

# NOTE: `contracts/fuzz/proptests/**/proptest-regressions/` is deliberately NOT
# ignored. proptest writes a counterexample there when a property fails, and
# replaying that seed on every subsequent run is the whole point of the file -
# it stops a found bug from silently returning once the input shrinks past what
# a random generator would produce. Commit them, the same as a fixture.

# cargo-fuzz coverage output
*.profraw
*.profdata
